    "q-148404": {
      "dom_id": "step-q148404",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Mike has a box with $7$ red LEGO blocks numbered from $1$ to $7$ and other $7$ blue LEGO blocks numbered from $8$ to $14.$ If Mike chooses a LEGO block at random, what is the probability that he picks a blue LEGO block?",
      "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the number on the chosen LEGO block. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U\\{1,2,…,14\\},$ and we wish to compute $P(8\\le X\\le 14).$\n\nIn general, if $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{1,2,…,14\\},$ and the set $S$ has $|S|=14$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{14}, & x=1,2,…,14 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ the items that satisfy $8\\le X\\le 14$ are $8,9,10,11,12,13,14.$ There are $7$ of these items. Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(8\\le X\\le 14)=7\\cdot \\frac{1}{14}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
