    "q-148407": {
      "dom_id": "step-q148407",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Maria collects stickers for a sticker album, where each sticker in the album has a different number on it.\nSo far, Maria has duplicates of the following sticker numbers:\n\n$$\n7,\\,12,\\,28,\\,35,\\,78,\\,81,\\,99,\\,112\n$$\n\nIf Maria picks a duplicate sticker at random to give to a friend, what is the probability that the sticker number she picks is greater than $70?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the number on the chosen sticker. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U\\{7,\\,12,\\,28,\\,35,\\,78,\\,81,\\,99,\\,112\\},$ and we wish to compute $P(X>70).$\n\nIn general, if $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{7,\\,12,\\,28,\\,35,\\,78,\\,81,\\,99,\\,112\\},$ and the set $S=\\{7,\\,12,\\,28,\\,35,\\,78,\\,81,\\,99,\\,112\\}$ has $|S|=8$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{8}, & x=7,\\,12,\\,28,\\,35,\\,78,\\,81,\\,99,\\,112 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ the items that satisfy $X>70$ are $78,\\,81,\\,99,\\,112.$ There are $4$ of these items. Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(X>70)=4\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}=\\frac{4}{8}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
